# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Your library — never commit this.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# library.db holds every note and tag you have ever written in this app. It is
# personal, irreplaceable, and has no business in a public repo. The -wal/-shm
# files are the live WAL sidecars; they are transient but can contain
# not-yet-checkpointed pages of the same data.
library.db
library.db-wal
library.db-shm
library.backup-*.db
backup-*.db

# Belt and braces: any sqlite file anywhere in the tree.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PDFs — copyrighted, large, and not yours to redistribute.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The directory itself is tracked (via papers/.gitkeep) so a fresh clone still
# has somewhere for the app to write uploads.
papers/*
!papers/.gitkeep
*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# This project is stdlib-only and needs no virtualenv, but people make them.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing in this app currently reads an API key — the chat pane shells out to
# the `claude` CLI and uses that CLI's own stored credentials, which live in
# your home directory, not here. These rules exist so that stays true even if
# someone later swaps in a direct API backend.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
.netrc
credentials.json
secrets.json
*secret*
*_token
.mcp.json

# Claude Code / agent tooling: share .claude/settings.json if you want, but
# never the machine-local one, which can hold paths and per-machine config.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/local/
.claude/todos/
.claude/shell-snapshots/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.*.sw[a-p]
*~
\#*\#
.\#*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# File-sync droppings (in case the tree lives in a synced folder)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.stfolder/
.stversions/
*.sync-conflict-*
.nextcloudsync.log
.~lock.*#

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LaTeX build artifacts, in case you point --draft at a .tex inside the repo
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.synctex.gz
*.toc

# The Librarian (librarian/): your brief, its derived data, caches and secrets.
# All of this is about YOUR research and stays out of the repo. librarian.db is
# covered by *.db above. Only the *.template.md files are tracked.
librarian/brief.md
librarian/gold_set.md
librarian/gold_report.md
librarian/LIBRARY.md
librarian/notes/
librarian/cache/
librarian/work/
librarian/.env
librarian/.venv/
